    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "[auto-routed: surprise=1.00] Implement the bootstrap rigidity test for small feedforward networks by constructing a linear constraint family (rigid/low-dimensional solution space) and scanning network width h to measure N_c(w) vs. constraint count w. Use scipy.optimize.minimize (L-BFGS-B) for training, multiple random seeds, and enforce zero-violation criteria (val_err ≤ 1e-3, train_err ≤ 1e-4). First validate zero-violation reachability at anchor point (w_min, h_max), then perform full scan to determine if N_c(w) is flat/decreasing (supports rigidity) or increasing (supports fat space)."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "None"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "For linear constraints (rigid), N_c(w) should be flat or decreasing as w increases; anchor point should achieve val_err ≤ 1e-3 and train_err ≤ 1e-4 at h=20, w=1. The trend classification will be \"不增（flat or decreasing）\" supporting rigid solution space."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
